      "text": "   1. **Finding the Reference Angle:**\n   - The angle $\\frac{11\\pi}{3}$ is typically measured in radians.\n   - To find the equivalent positive angle within the range of $0$ to $2\\pi$, we reduce $\\frac{11\\pi}{3}$ modulo $2\\pi$:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{11\\pi}{3} \\mod 2\\pi = \\frac{11\\pi}{3} - 2\\pi = \\frac{11\\pi}{3} - \\frac{6\\pi}{3} = \\frac{5\\pi}{3}.\n     \\]\n\n2. **Sign of the Sine Function for the Obtained Angle:**\n   - The sine function undergoes a sign change within the interval $(-\\pi, 0)$ and $(\\pi, 2\\pi)$.\n   - The equivalent angle $\\frac{5\\pi}{3}$ falls in the interval:\n     \\[\n     \\pi < \\frac{5\\pi}{3} < 2\\pi.\n     \\]\n\n3. **Simplifying the Calculator's Output:**\n   - Using calculator functions, we get:\n     \\begin{align*}\n     \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) &\\approx -\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3} - 2\\pi\\right) \\\\\n                     &\\approx -\\sin\\left(\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\\n                     &\\approx -\\sin\\left(2\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\\n                     &\\approx -\\left(-\\sin\\left(-\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n                     &\\approx \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) \\\\\n                     &\\approx 0.866.\n     \\end{align*}\n   \n   - Therefore, the sine of $\\frac{11\\pi}{3}$ is given by:\n     \\[\n     \\boxed{0.866}\n     \\]",
